":"Using LiveQuery","anchor":"Using-LiveQuery"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LiveQuery"},{"text":" is a SwiftUI property wrapper that keeps your view state in sync","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with SwiftData. It refreshes when the underlying model container saves, so your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lists and sections stay current without manual fetch logic.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It can be thought of as an alternative to SwiftData’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Query"},{"text":" macro, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"explicit dependency-based context configuration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@LiveQuery"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" models (for example, a feature","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"model that owns shared data) and any other main-actor-isolated type where you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"want live SwiftData-backed state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When using ","type":"text"},{"code":"@LiveQuery","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" model, mark the property","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@ObservationIgnored","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to avoid conflicts with the Observation framework:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["@Observable","final class MyFeatureModel {","    @ObservationIgnored","    @LiveQuery var items: [Item]","}"]}],"name":"Note","style":"note","type":"aside"},{"text":"Configure the ModelContext (primary)","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Configure-the-ModelContext-primary"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@LiveQuery","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" relies on the Dependencies value ","type":"text"},{"code":"liveQueryContext.modelContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Configure it once at your app entry point so every view has a consistent source"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of truth. This is the recommended setup for most apps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you do not already have a container, create a main container up front and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass its "},{"code":"mainContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" into the dependency:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Dependencies","import SwiftData","import SwiftDataHelpers","import SwiftUI","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    let container: ModelContainer = try! ModelContainer(","        for: Person.self","    )","","    init() {","        let container = self.container","        prepareDependencies {","            $0.liveQueryContext.modelContext = { container.mainContext }","        }","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .modelContainer(container)","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Use-LiveQuery","text":"Use @LiveQuery","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@LiveQuery","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps SwiftUI in sync with SwiftData by refreshing when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"underlying container saves. You can pass a predicate and sort descriptors to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"filter and order results.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftDataHelpers","import SwiftUI","","struct PeopleList: View {","    @LiveQuery(","        predicate: #Predicate<Person> { $0.isActive },","        sort: [SortDescriptor(\\Person.name)]","    )","    private var people: [Person]","","    var body: some View {","        List(people) { person in","            Text(person.name)","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Consume-LiveQuery-as-AsyncStream","text":"Consume LiveQuery as AsyncStream","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$people.valuesStream"},{"text":" when you need async iteration over snapshots:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this pattern is primarily for non-UIKit types (for example, ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"models). For UIKit controllers, prefer ","type":"text"},{"code":"LiveQueryViewController","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LiveQueryViewController\/observe(_:onSnapshot:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@MainActor","@Observable","final class PeopleFeatureModel {","    @ObservationIgnored","    @LiveQuery(sort: [SortDescriptor(\\Person.name)])","    var people: [Person]","","    @ObservationIgnored","    private var valuesTask: Task<Void, Never>?","","    func observePeople() {","        valuesTask?.cancel()","        valuesTask = Task {","            for await snapshot in $people.valuesStream {","                print(\"People count: \\(snapshot.count)\")","            }","        }","    }","","    deinit {","        valuesTask?.cancel()","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Use LiveQuery in UIKit View Controllers","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Use-LiveQuery-in-UIKit-View-Controllers"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For UIKit screens, subclass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LiveQueryViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" and register projected"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"queries with "},{"code":"LiveQueryViewController\/observe(_:onSnapshot:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The base class"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"starts observation in ","type":"text"},{"code":"viewDidAppear","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and stops it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewDidDisappear"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftDataHelpers","import UIKit","","final class PeopleViewController: LiveQueryViewController {","    @LiveQuery(sort: [SortDescriptor(\\Person.name)])","    private var people: [Person]","","    private var displayedPeople: [Person] = []","    private let tableView = UITableView(frame: .zero, style: .plain)","","    override func viewDidLoad() {","        super.viewDidLoad()","","        observe($people) { [weak self] snapshot in","            guard let self else { return }","            displayedPeople = snapshot","            tableView.reloadData()","        }","    }","}"]},{"text":"Multiple Containers (optional)","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Multiple-Containers-optional"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your app uses more than one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ModelContainer"},{"type":"text","text":" (for example, main and private"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores), use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDataHelpers\/documentation\/SwiftDataHelpers\/LiveQueryBindable"},{"type":"text","text":" to scope queries to the desired container."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This is ideal for subtrees of your UI that should read from a non-default"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"container."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["LiveQueryBindable(modelContainer: .privatePersons) {","    PrivatePeopleView()","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Previews-and-Tests-optional","text":"Previews and Tests (optional)","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For previews and tests, inject a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ModelContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly. This keeps ","type":"text"},{"code":"@LiveQuery","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"functional without bootstrapping your full app lifecycle.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["#Preview {","    prepareDependencies {","        $0.liveQueryContext.modelContext = { ModelContainer.main.mainContext }","    }","","    return PeopleList()","        .modelContainer(.main)","}"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"FAQ","text":"FAQ","type":"heading"},{"level":3,"anchor":"I-see-logs-about-liveQueryContextmodelContext-not-set-What-does-it-mean","text":"I see logs about `liveQueryContext.modelContext` not set. What does it mean?","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@LiveQuery","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" requires a "},{"code":"ModelContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDataHelpers\/documentation\/SwiftDataHelpers\/Dependencies\/DependencyValues\/liveQueryContext","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"If this dependency is not configured, SwiftDataHelpers logs a fault and the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"query returns empty results until a context is provided. Configure it once at","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"your app entry point with "},{"code":"prepareDependencies","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or scope a subtree with"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftDataHelpers\/documentation\/SwiftDataHelpers\/LiveQueryBindable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Can-I-use-LiveQuery-outside-of-views","text":"Can I use `@LiveQuery` outside of views?","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inl